# logs/trade_log.csv and logs/equity_log.csv are append-only: every
# scheduled run may add one new row at the end. Two workflows (crypto,
# stocks) committing to the same file within moments of each other is
# normal, not an error - but git's default merge treats two independent
# appends at the same end-of-file position as a conflict, since it can't
# tell they don't actually overlap. Confirmed live on 2026-07-28: this
# produced a DETERMINISTIC rebase conflict that failed identically on
# every retry (not a timing race - retrying the exact same rebase can
# never resolve a real content conflict). `merge=union` tells git to
# just keep both sides' added lines instead of flagging a conflict -
# verified locally that this resolves the exact reproduced conflict
# cleanly, preserving both rows in order.
logs/trade_log.csv merge=union
logs/equity_log.csv merge=union
